# -*- coding: utf-8 -*-
"""Write the hand-researched domains for Heimtextil, TISE and Coverings.

Same method and same columns as tcna_domains.csv: web search over each
company's own indexed pages, never Clay. gate_flag carries the free verdict
that fell out of the research, so rows that cannot pass S7.4 are visible
before any credit is spent.

confidence values:
  high    - the company's own site appeared in results and the city, country
            or business description cross-checks against the directory row
  medium  - a domain is named, but only by a directory or a summary, with no
            independent hit on the site itself. Verify before spending credits
  none    - searched twice, no website exists. Directory or marketplace only
  unresolved - the name is too generic or too thinly indexed to pin down.
            Needs the exhibitor listing itself
"""
import csv

# 'state' held a US state code on some rows and an ISO country code on others,
# which is the exact ambiguity that produced the Bisazza VI bug three times
# (Vicenza province read as Virgin Islands). Two-letter codes collide badly:
# ID is Idaho and Indonesia, IL is Illinois and Israel, IN is Indiana and
# India, CA is California and Canada. So country is now its own column, set
# from the named subdivision map below rather than guessed from the code.
COLS = ['company','domain','alt_domain','city','state','country','confidence',
        'gate_flag','research_note']

# every row whose 'state' value is a US or Canadian subdivision, not a country
